ters 8 to 512+ GPUs, specific hardware, InfiniBand configs on request Supplier Matchmaking Spheron sources from its certified data center network, negotiates pricing, handles setup Tell us your GPU needs and we&#x27;ll match you with the right provider from our certified data center network. Request a Quote Typical turnaround: 24–48 hours FAQ / 06 Pricing FAQ 01 What&#x27;s included in the hourly GPU rate? The hourly rate covers everything you need to get started: a fully provisioned VM or bare metal instance with your selected GPU, high-speed NVMe SSD storage, network bandwidth, and a dedicated IP address with full root access. There are no hidden fees or surcharges. 02 Is there a minimum rental period? No, there is no minimum rental period. Spheron charges with per-minute billing granularity, so you only pay for the exact time you use. Spin up a GPU for a quick test run or keep it running for weeks — it’s entirely up to you. 03 Do you offer volume discounts? Yes, we offer competitive volume and enterprise pricing for teams that need multiple GPUs or long-term capacity. Contact our sales team to discuss your requirements and get a custom quote tailored to your workload. Contact sales → 04 What payment methods are accepted? We accept credit cards for traditional payments. We also support stables payments like USDT and USDC, making it easy to pay however you prefer. 05 Can I switch GPU models mid-project? Absolutely. You can spin down one GPU instance and spin up another model at any time. There are no lock-in periods or penalties for switching. This flexibility lets you use a cost-effective GPU for development and scale up to a more powerful one for production training. 06 How does pricing compare to AWS/GCP/Azure? Spheron’s GPU pricing is significantly cheaper than major cloud providers. For example, an H100 on Spheron starts at $1.33/hr compared to $6.98/hr on Azure and $7.00/hr on AWS (as of Q1 2026) — that’s 40–60% less than hyperscalers. Check our GPU-specific 