rage/manage-lifecycle-policies \\nVultr Archival Object Storage Product \\u0026 Support Documentation: https://docs.vultr.com/products/cloud-storage/object-storage/archival-storage \\n\\nTimestamps\\n0:00 – Introduction\\n0:59 – Vultr Archival Object Storage Tier\\n1:45 – Archival Storage in Standard Object Storage Tier\\n3:12 – Use Cases\\n4:23 – Demo Overview\\n4:55 – Provisioning Vultr Archival Object Storage\\n6:58 – Creating Buckets, Uploading, and Accessing Objects in Archival Object Storage\\n8:55 – Enabling Archival Storage in Standard Object Storage\\n10:04 – Customizing Lifecycle Policies\\n11:21 – Restoring Archived Objects\\n12:22 – Summary \\u0026 Getting Started\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"25:T65a,\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"Most DevOps workflows still rely on a fragmented toolchain, where translating intent into reliable execution requires both context and precision. This gap between what you want done and what actually gets executed on infrastructure remains one of the biggest sources of friction in modern development. In this tech talk, we explore how OpenClaw, using Vultr's Marketplace Apps, approaches this problem by introducing a persistent, server-side AI agent that doesn’t just respond, but rather observes, executes, and maintains context over time.\\n\\nDeploy your own OpenClaw instance on Vultr and get $250 in free credits: https://www.vultr.com/promo/try250/ \\n\\nJoin the Vultr Community Forum to ask questions or connect with other developers:\\nhttps://community.vultr.com/ \\n\\nDocs \\u0026 Resources\\nOpenClaw Documentation: https://docs.openclaw.ai/ \\nVultr’s OpenClaw Marketplace Application: https://www.vultr.com/marketplace/apps/openclaw \\nHow to Use Vultr's OpenClaw Marketplace Application: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-use-vultrs-openclaw-marketplace-application \\nHow to Deploy OpenClaw – Autonomous AI Agent Platform: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-deploy-openclaw-autonomous-ai-agent-platform \\n\\nTimestamps\\n0:00 – Introduction\\n1:02 – The Gap Between Intent and Action\\n2:20 – OpenClaw\\n3:34 – Vultr’s OpenClaw Marketplace Application\\n4:53 – Demo Overview\\n5:14 – Provisioning OpenClaw on Vultr via Marketplace Apps\\n8:10 – Exploring OpenClaw Control UI\\n11:34 – Interacting \\u0026 Building a Sample Application with OpenClaw\\n12:33 – Verifying the Generated Application on Code Server\\n15:24 – Summary \\u0026 Getting Started\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"26:T7fc,\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"Large language models have outgrown single-node inference. Serving them efficiently at scale demands careful orchestration across GPU fleets, intelligent memory management, and real-time resource planning. In this tech talk, we take a deep dive into NVIDIA Dynamo. We walk through disaggregated serving, KV cache-aware smart routing, supported open-source inference backends, GPU resource planning with SLA-driven autoscaling, and full-stack observability with Prometheus and Grafana.\\n\\nGet started with NVIDIA Dynamo on Vultr GPU instances by claiming $250 in free credits on a new account: https://www.vultr.com/promo/try250/\\n\\nTo participate in discussions or ask questions, join the Vultr Community Forum: https://community.vultr.com/ \\n\\nDocs \\u0026 Resources\\n\\nHow to Build Disaggregated Inference with NVIDIA Dynamo: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-build-disaggregated-inference-with-nvidia-dynamo\\nHow to Configure Smart Routing in NVIDIA Dynamo: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-configure-smart-routing-in-nvidia-dynamo\\nHow to Manage KV Cache in NVIDIA Dynamo: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-manage-kv-cache-in-nvidia-dynamo \\nHow to Deploy Inference using NVIDIA Dynamo and vLLM: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-deploy-inference-using-nvidia-dynamo-and-vllm \\nHow to Deploy Inference using NVIDIA Dynamo and SGLang: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-deploy-inference-using-nvidia-dynamo-and-sglang \\nHow to Deploy Inference using NVIDIA Dynamo and TensorRT-LLM: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-deploy-inference-using-nvidia-dynamo-and-tensorrt-llm \\nHow to Optimize GPU Resource Planning with NVIDIA Dynamo: https://docs.vultr.com/how-to-optimize-gpu-resource-planning-with-nvidia-dynamo \\nNVIDIA Dynamo Official Documentation: https://docs.nvidia.com/dynamo/latest/getting-started/quickstart \\n\\nTimestamps\\n0:00 – Introduction\\n1:00 – NVIDIA Dynamo\\n2:07 – Disaggregated Serving\\n3:18 – KV Smart Router \\u0026 KV Cache Manager\\n5:03 – Supported Inference Backends\\n6:11 – GPU Resource Planner\\n7:21 – Observability \\u0026 Monitoring\\n8:21 – Summary \\u0026 Getting Started\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"27:T78c,\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"PostgreSQL is one of the most powerful open-source database engines available today. But running it reliably in a production environment means managing replication, failover, backups, connection handling, and performance monitoring, all while keeping the database secure and continuously available. In this tech talk, we break down how Vultr’s Managed Databases for PostgreSQL delivers a fully managed cluster architecture see how its capabilities translate into real application workflows.\\n\\nGet started with Vultr Managed PostgreSQL by claiming $250 in free credits on a new account: https://www.vultr.com/promo/try250/ \\n\\nTo participate in discussions or ask questions, join the Vultr Community Forum: https://community.vultr.com/ \\n\\nDocs \\u0026 Resources\\nVultr Managed Databases for PostgreSQL documentation: https://docs.vultr.com/products/managed-database/postgresql \\nExplore all Vultr Managed Databases: https://docs.vultr.com/products/managed-database \\n[Tech Talk] Architecting Scalable Applications with Vultr Managed Databases for MySQL: https://youtu.be/VUSCKOMMk8o\\n[Tech Talk] Web Application Caching with Vultr Managed Databases for Valkey: https://youtu.be/nnanIO954K0\\n[Tech Talk] Ingesting Kafka Topics in Applications with Vultr Managed Apache Kafka® Connect: https://youtu.be/osZCG-awclo\\nLearn more about provisioning and managing Vultr VPCs: https://docs.vultr.com/products/network/vpc | https://youtu.be/N_lwBdgW-1c\\n\\nTimestamps\\n0:00 – Introduction\\n1:12 – Vultr’s Managed Databases for PostgreSQL\\n2:20 – Vultr Managed PostgreSQL Connections and Capabilities\\n3:53 – Use Cases\\n5:08 – Demo Overview\\n5:38 – Provisioning Vultr Managed PostgreSQL Database Cluster\\n8:14 – Connecting Product Catalog Application with PostgreSQL Cluster\\n13:30 – Verifying Connection and Performing Real-Time Actions in the Interface\\n15:18 – Exploring Vultr Managed PostgreSQL Capabilities\\n21:36 – Summary \\u0026 Getting Started\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"28:T5d2,\"]) self.__next_f.push([1,\"Running MySQL in production involves far more than simply launching a database instance. You must design for high availability, automated backups, secure connectivity, replication, monitoring, and seamless scaling, all while minimizing operational overhead. In this tech talk, we explore how Vultr’s Managed Databases for MySQL addresses these challenges and simplifies running MySQL in production environments.\\n\\nGet started with Vultr Managed Databases for MySQL by claiming $250 in free credits on a new account: https://www.vultr.com/promo/try250/ \\n\\nTo participate in discussions and ask questions, join the Vultr Community Forum: https://community.vultr.com/ \\n\\nDocs \\u0026 Resources\\nVultr Managed Databases for MySQL documentation: https://docs.vultr.com/products/managed-database/mysql\\nExplore Vultr Managed PostgreSQL, Valkey, and Apache alongside MySQL Databases: https://docs.vultr.com/products/managed-database\\nLearn more about provisioning and managing Vultr VPCs: https://docs.vultr.com/products/network/vpc | https://youtu.be/N_lwBdgW-1c \\n\\nTimestamps\\n0:00 – Introduction\\n1:09 – Vultr’s Managed Databases for MySQL\\n2:34 – Vultr Managed MySQL Database Architecture\\n4:05 – Use Cases\\n5:50 – Demo Overview\\n6:23 – Provisioning Vultr Managed MySQL\\n8:31 – Connecting Task Manager A