h((row, index) => { if (showAllRows || index Heads up: We do our best to keep these prices accurate. However, cloud costs may fluctuate based on region, usage, and other factors not listed here. These are estimates based on common setups and are for informational purposes only. Always verify current rates with the provider before provisioning. Frequently Asked Questions Why choose the MI300X? Comes with 192GB HBM3 - the largest memory of any single GPU. 5.3 TB/s memory bandwidth. Strong ROCm ecosystem for PyTorch workloads. Competitive pricing against H100 for inference. When is the MI300X not a good fit? ROCm software ecosystem, while rapidly improving, is narrower than CUDA. Some frameworks and libraries may have limited AMD support. Multi-node training tooling is less mature than Nvidia's. Are MI300X prices going up or down? On-demand pricing has increased by about 33% since May 2025, from $2.35 to $3.12/hr per GPU. What size AI models can the MI300X run? With 192GB of VRAM, the MI300X can usually run 70B-class models with headroom, and may handle much larger models in 4-bit quantized form depending on runtime overhead, KV cache, and context length. How much VRAM does the MI300X have? The MI300X has 192GB of VRAM. Multi-GPU setups increase total memory, but that memory is not automatically pooled across GPUs. What is the MI300X&#x27;s memory bandwidth? The MI300X has 5,300 GB/s of memory bandwidth. Higher bandwidth helps with faster data transfer between GPU memory and compute cores. What data types does the MI300X support? The MI300X supports 6 precision formats. Training: BF16, FP16, FP32. Inference: FP8, INT8. Scientific: FP64. Does the MI300X support Infinity Fabric? Yes. The MI300X supports Infinity Fabric with 896 GB/s of bidirectional bandwidth. This helps accelerate multi-GPU communication. How much does the MI300X cost per hour? MI300X pricing currently ranges from $0.95/hr to $7.86/hr per GPU, depending on the provider, instance type, and billing model. How much does the MI300X cost per month? At 720 hours per month, one MI300X can cost between $684.00 to $5,656.77 per month, depending on the provider. Reserved and spot pricing can lower that further. Which cloud providers offer the MI300X? The MI300X is available from 9 cloud providers, including Cirrascale, DigitalOcean, Crusoe. Pricing and availability vary by region and billing model. Can I rent the MI300X in the cloud? Yes. We currently track 21 MI300X listings across 9 cloud providers: Billing type Listings Avg $/GPU/hr On-demand 9 $3.25/hr Reserved 8 $3.10/hr Spot 2 $1.20/hr Custom contract 2 On request Technical Specifications TF32 (TFLOPs) 653.7 FP16 (TFLOPs) 1307.4 BFLOAT16 (TFLOPs) 1307.4 INT8 (TOPS) 2614.9 FP8 (TFLOPs) 2614.9 FP64 vector 81.7 FP32 vector 163.4 FP64 matrix 163.4 FP32 matrix 163.4 Decoders 4 groups for HEVC/H.265, AVC/H.264, V1, or AV1 JPEG/MJPEG CODEC 32 cores, 8 cores per group Virtualization support SR-IOV, up to 8 partitions Form factor OAM module Lithography 5nm FinFET, 6nm FinFET GPU compute units 304 Matrix cores 1216 Stream processors 19,456 Peak engine clock 2100 MHz Memory capacity Up to 192 GB HBM3 Memory bandwidth 5.3 TB/s max. peak theoretical Memory interface 8192 bits AMD Infinity Cache™ (last level) 256 MB Memory clock Up to 5.2 GT/s Scale-up Infinity Fabric™ Links 7x 128 GB/s I/O to host CPU 1 PCIe® Gen 5 x16 (128 GB/s) Scale-out network bandwidth PCIe Gen 5 x16 (128 GB/s) RAS features Full-chip ECC memory, page retirement, page avoidance Maximum TBP 750W Source: official AMD MI300X datasheet . Alternatives to AMD MI300X Nvidia H100 NVIDIA alternative with CUDA ecosystem. From $0.47/hr per GPU across 43 providers. AMD MI325X Next generation with 33% more memory. From $2.00/hr per GPU across 3 providers. Nvidia A100 NVIDIA Ampere alternative. From $0.13/hr per GPU across 38 providers. Last updated May 25, 2026 GPUhub Our sponsor Fully Dedicated GPU Servers No Virtualization. No Shared GPUs Stable Performance for AI Traini