upermicro\" } } { \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [ { \"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What makes Supermicro unique for AI servers?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Supermicro offers 100+ GPU server configurations using Building Block Solutions® architecture, significantly more than competitors (typically 10-20). They have 4-6 week lead times, support for NVIDIA, AMD, and Intel accelerators, and DLC-2 liquid cooling achieving 40% power savings.\" } }, { \"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the Supermicro GB200 NVL72 SuperCluster?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The GB200 NVL72 SuperCluster is a complete rack-scale AI system with 72 NVIDIA B200/B300 GPUs and 36 Grace CPUs. It delivers 1+ ExaFLOPS FP8 performance with 13.8TB+ HBM3e memory in a single rack. Price range is $3M-$4M per rack system.\" } }, { \"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What Supermicro AI server models are available?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Key models include the 4U liquid-cooled SYS-421GE-TNHR2-LCC (8x H200/B200, $350K-$500K), 8U air-cooled SYS-821GE-TNHR ($250K-$350K), and AMD Instinct AS-8125GS-TNMR2 (8x MI300X, $300K-$400K). SuperBlade and Intel Gaudi 3 platforms are also available.\" } }, { \"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is Supermicro DLC-2 liquid cooling?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"DLC-2 is Supermicro's second-generation direct liquid cooling technology that cools GPUs, CPUs, DIMMs, VRMs and PCIe switches. It achieves 40% power savings versus air cooling, 20% TCO reduction, supports 250kW heat removal per rack, and enables 4U form factor for 8 B200 GPUs.\" } }, { \"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How fast can Supermicro servers be delivered?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Supermicro offers industry-leading 4-6 week standard lead times thanks to Building Block Solutions® 