":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"AceCloud\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/acecloud.ai\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/07\\/acecloud-by-rtds-black-logo.svg\"}},\"datePublished\":\"2025-08-26\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-03-11\"} Cloud GPU Pricing Comparison in India [2026] Jason Karlin Last Updated: Mar 11, 2026 8 Minute Read 4195 Views Table of Contents Subscribe to our newsletter Get latest updates, tips, and exclusive offers in your inbox. Subscribe By subscribing, you agree to our Privacy Policy . Share AI is moving from pilots to production and GPU spend is fast becoming a board-level line item. Hence, we have compared cloud GPU providers in India (INR) like AceCloud, AWS, Google Cloud, Microsoft Azure, DigitalOcean and E2E Networks. Our aim is practical, not theoretical. We want you to match workloads to GPU classes (H100/A100/L40S/L4/A30/RTX) and understand the budget impact of hourly and monthly Cloud GPU pricing options. So, read this as a TCO starting point, i.e., figures reflect listed prices in INR*, excluding taxes, network egress, sustained use or commitment discounts and Spot/Preemptible variability. We highly recommend you use it to set envelopes for FY25-26 planning, negotiate supplier terms and choose the right mix of cost, performance and control for each workload. Let’s get started! AceCloud (Hourly Pricing) AceCloud provides pay-as-you-go GPU servers aimed at AI training, fine-tuning, inference, rendering and data science. You can match GPUs to workload needs (from high-end H100 to cost-savvy A2/L4) and size CPU/RAM alongside them. Model Flavor Name GPUs vCPUs RAM (GB) Hourly* NVIDIA H100 – HGX N.HGXH100.250 1 26 250 ₹315.07 NVIDIA A100 N.A100.128 1 16 128 ₹184.93 NVIDIA A30 N.A30.32 1 8 32 ₹71.92 NVIDIA A2 N.A2.32 1 8 32 ₹23.01 RTX A6000 N.RTXA6000.64 1 16 64 ₹59.08 NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada N.RTX6000ADA.64 1 16 64 ₹84.28 NVIDIA L4 N.L4.32 1 8 32 ₹41.92 NVIDIA L40S N.L40S.64 1 16 64 ₹123.29 Instances can be spun up quickly, scaled or paused as projects evolve and paired with containers or your preferred ML frameworks. The goal is predictable performance with transparent INR pricing so teams can budget experiments and production runs without surprises. * You can avail these instances at hourly rates if your billing reaches 200+ hours. Connect with AceCloud’s Cloud GPU consultant using free consultation to learn more. Amazon AWS (Hourly Pricing) AWS Cloud GPU services deliver managed, on-demand accelerators for training, inference and visualization, integrating with EC2, EKS, autoscaling and spot pricing. Model Storage vCPU Memory Hourly Billing (H100) P5.4xlarge 1 x 3840 GB SSD 16 256 GiB ₹720.33 (A100) P4d.24xlarge 8 x 1000 SSD 96 1152 GiB ₹2298.52 (L4) G6.xlarge 1 x 250 GB NVMe SSD 4 16 GiB ₹84.32 Choose H100 for cutting-edge training, A100 for large multi-GPU workloads and L4 for cost-efficient inference or graphics. Management is via familiar AWS tooling. Google GCP (Hourly Pricing) Google Cloud GPU services provide on-demand accelerators for training, inference and visualization across Vertex AI, GKE and Compute Engine, with flexible pricing, autoscaling and Spot options. Model Region Hourly Billing A100 80GB Mumbai ₹491.534806 H100 Mumbai ₹1,061.454025 L4 Mumbai ₹60.735897 You can integrate with Google’s secure networking, storage and observability stacks and enforce budgets via labels and quotas. Managed images and NVIDIA MIG profiles simplify right-sizing, tenancy and isolation. Microsoft Azure (Hourly Pricing) Microsoft Azure GPU services provide on-demand NVIDIA accelerators via NC/ND-series VMs, integrated with Azure Machine Learning, AKS, VM Scale Sets, Spot capacity and reservation pricing. Model vCPUs RAM Temp storage GPU Hourly Billing H100 NC40ads v5 40 320 GiB 3,576 GiB 1× H100 ₹848.4050 A100 NC24ads v4 24 220 GiB 958 GiB 1× A100 ₹446.4284 Management hooks include Azure Policy, budgets/tags and role-based access control, with images and (where available) MIG to right-size inference and training. DigitalOcean (Hourly Pricing) DigitalOcean GPU Droplets offer straightforward, hourly pricing and a simple developer experience. Spin up single-GPU instances for training, fine-tuning, inference or graphics, then scale with DOKS (Kubernetes), VPC networking, block storage and monitoring. Model GPU memory (total) Droplet memory vCPUs Boot disk Hourly Billing H200 141 GB 240 GiB 24 720 GiB NVMe ₹300.15 H100 80 GB 240 GiB 20 720 GiB NVMe ₹588.09 RTX 6000 Ada 48 GB 64 GiB 8 500 GiB NVMe ₹136.99 L40S 48 GB 64 GiB 8 500 GiB NVMe ₹136.99 Teams can use projects, tags and budgets to track spend; snapshots and reserved IPs ease lifecycle management. E2E Networks (Hourly Pricing) E2E Networks offers India-based GPU Dedicated Compute with simple, INR-denominated hourly pricing, which is handy for teams training, fine-tuning or running inference close to users in the region. Plans span cutting-edge H200/H100 to value options like L4 and A30. Model GPU Memory vCPUs Ded RAM (GB) Disk Space Hourly Billing H200 Plans 141 GB 30 375 3750 GB NVMe ₹183 H100 Plans 80 GB 26 250 3000 GB NVMe ₹175 A100 80GB 4 × 80 GB 64 460 250 GB SSD ₹400 L40S 1 × 48 GB 25 220 250 GB SSD ₹83 A30 1 × 24 GB 16 90 640 GB SSD ₹96 L4 1 × 24 GB 25 110 250 GB SSD ₹50 You can choose single-GPU nodes for experiments or multi-GPU A100 for heavier training. The specs are straightforward (fixed vCPUs, RAM and NVMe/SSD), so it’s easy to estimate cost and performance without surprises. If you want a complete bill estimate beyond GPU-hour pricing (compute, storage, and network/egress), follow our step-by-step cloud cost estimation guide . Cloud GPU Monthly Pricing Comparison in India Below is a side-by-side comparison of cloud GPU pricing, organized by GPU model across major providers. NVIDIA H100 (Monthly Pricing) For an 8× H100 (80 GB each) monthly setup, AceCloud costs ₹16 lakh. AWS is ~₹42.9 lakh, Azure ~₹38.6 lakh and Google Cloud ~₹58.8 lakh. Feature AceCloud E2E Networks Google Cloud AWS Azure Digital Ocean GPUs 8 8 8 8 8 8 vCPU 208 200 208 192 96 160 RAM 2000GB 1800GB 1872GB 2040GB 1900GB 1920GB vRAM 8 * 80GB 8 * 80GB 8 * 80GB 8 * 80GB 8 * 80GB 8 * 80GB Monthly Billing ₹16,00,000 (No hidden fees) ₹16,76,000 ₹58,79,378 ₹42,92,377 ₹38,58,540 ₹16,42,751 Support 24/7 Dedicated Human Support (No Bots) Limited support Paid support plans Paid support plans Paid support plans Paid support plans Free Credits ₹20,000 Free credits ₹17,000 ₹25,000 ₹17,000 ₹17,000 ₹17,000 That makes AceCloud roughly 63% cheaper than AWS, 59% cheaper than Azure and 73% cheaper than GCP, saving about ₹27 lakh vs AWS, ₹22.6 lakh vs Azure and ₹42.8 lakh vs GCP each month. For a detailed buy vs rent breakdown, plus India purchase ranges and where to buy, read our NVIDIA H100 price in India guide. NVIDIA A100 (Monthly Pricing) For an A100 monthly setup (per your table), AceCloud costs ₹3.6 lakh. AWS is ~₹17.56 lakh and Google Cloud ~₹15.54 lakh; Azure price wasn’t available at the time of writing. Feature AceCloud E2E Networks Google Cloud AWS Azure Digital Ocean vCPU 64 64 48 96 96 – GPUs 4 4 4 8 8 – RAM 512GB 460GB 680GB 1152GB 900GB – vRAM 4 * 80GB 4 * 80GB 4 * 80GB 8 * 80GB 8 * 80GB – Monthly Billing ₹360,000 (No hidden fees) ₹400,000 ₹15,53,958 ₹17,55,972 N/A – Support 24/7 Dedicated Human Support (No Bots) Limited support Paid support plans Paid support plans Paid support plans – Free Credits ₹20,000 Free credits ₹17,000 ₹25,000 ₹17,000 ₹17,000 – That makes AceCloud about 79.5% cheaper than AWS and 76.8% cheaper than GCP, saving roughly ₹14.0 lakh vs AWS and ₹11.9 lakh vs GCP each month. Get A100 at Unbeatable Monthly Price on AceCloud NVIDIA L4 (Monthly Pricing) For a single NVIDIA L4 (24 GB) monthly setup, AceCloud costs ₹27,500. AWS is ~₹102,672 and Google Cloud ~₹76,000. Feature AceCloud E2E Networks Google Cloud AWS Azure Digital Ocean vCPU 16 25 16 16 – – GPUs 1 1 1 1 – – RAM 64GB 110GB 64GB 64GB – – vRAM 1 * 24GB 1 * 24GB 1 * 24GB 1 * 24GB – – Monthly Billing ₹27,