eature AceCloud E2E Networks Google Cloud AWS Azure Digital Ocean vCPU 8 – – – – – GPUs 1 – – – – – RAM 32GB – – – – – vRAM 1 * 16GB – – – – – Monthly Billing ₹12,000 (No hidden fees) – – – – – Support 24/7 Dedicated Human Support (No Bots) – – – – – Free Credits ₹20,000 Free credits – – – – – Try Nvidia A2 GPUs Only on AceCloud NVIDIA RTX A6000 (Monthly Pricing) For NVIDIA RTX A6000, only AceCloud is the contender for Cloud GPU service in India. Feature AceCloud E2E Networks Google Cloud AWS Azure Digital Ocean vCPU 16 – – – – – GPUs 1 – – – – – RAM 64GB – – – – – vRAM 1 * 48GB – – – – – Monthly Billing ₹37,500 (No hidden fees) – – – – – Support 24/7 Dedicated Human Support (No Bots) – – – – – Free Credits ₹20,000 Free credits – – – – – Rent RTX A6000 At AceCloud’s Lowest Rate NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada (Monthly Pricing) For a single NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada (48 GB) monthly setup, AceCloud costs ₹53,500. DigitalOcean is ~₹1,02,106. Feature AceCloud E2E Networks Google Cloud AWS Azure Digital Ocean vCPU 16 – – – – 8 GPUs 1 – – – – 1 RAM 64GB – – – – 64GB vRAM 1 * 48GB – – – – 1 * 48GB Monthly Billing ₹53,500 (No hidden fees) – – – – ₹1,02,106 Support 24/7 Dedicated Human Support (No Bots) – – – – Paid support plans Free Credits ₹20,000 Free credits – – – – ₹17,000 That makes AceCloud roughly 48% cheaper, saving about ₹48,606 per month. Prices for E2E Networks, Google Cloud, AWS and Azure weren’t available at the time of writing. Rent RTX 6000 Ada at Unbeatable Pricing with AceCloud Stay Cost-Effective, Choose AceCloud! Enterprise buyers should anchor decisions in unit economics (₹/GPU-hour or ₹/training run) and operational fit. From the comparison, AceCloud and E2E often deliver the lowest INR prices for equivalent GPUs. This is particularly true for H100 and L4 while AWS, Azure and GCP command higher rates but offer deeper ecosystems, multi-region scale and managed services. We suggest a pragmatic path: Classify workloads (cutting-edge training, mainstream training or inference/graphics), Right-size GPUs (H100/A100 vs L40S/L4/A30), Pilot on two providers to baseline performance and stability, Model full TCO including storage, inter-AZ traffic, egress, support tiers and commitments, and Enforce FinOps, i.e., budgets, tags and cost per request/token. If lowering ₹/GPU-hour is a priority, start a short PoC on AceCloud (e.g., H100 for training, L4/L40S for inference), use the ₹20,000 credits noted above and request a tailored INR quote with capacity planning and FinOps guardrails. Engage AceCloud to benchmark your workloads and lock in predictable monthly spending! *The hourly and monthly rates in the post are from Feb 2026. The details are subject to changing exchange rates, data center regions and resource availability across Cloud GPU providers. Author Popular Post Jason Karlin author Industry veteran with over 10 years of experience architecting and managing GPU-powered cloud solutions. Specializes in enabling scalable AI/ML and HPC workloads for enterprise and research applications. Former lead solutions architect for top-tier cloud providers and startups in the AI infrastructure space. CUDA cores vs Tensor cores: Choosing the Right GPU for Machine Learning GPUs in Healthcare: Transforming Diagnoses and Treatment with Cutting-Edge Technology The New Wave of Cloud GPUs: Revolutionizing the Business Landscape Harnessing GPU-as-a-Service: Key Benefits and Future Trends Best GPUs For Deep Learning [2025 Updated List] Related Post Explore trends, industry updates, and expert opinions to drive your business forward. Blog, Cloud GPU, NVIDIA A100, NVIDIA L4 Dec 20, 2024 NVIDIA A100 vs L4: Which is the Right GPU for Your Workload? Learn More Blog, Cloud GPU Oct 4, 2023 Cloud GPUs: The Cornerstone of Modern AI Learn More Finance Mar 19, 2024 How Are GPUs Unlocking Advanced AI Capabilities in Banking? Learn More Cloud GPU Nov 7, 2025 NVIDIA B200 vs H200, H100 & A100: Complete GPU Comparison Learn More Blog, Cloud GPU Sep 17, 2024 GPU vs. CPU: Whi